Feature 7 is complete. Here's how to test it:

---

## Testing Feature 7: Transaction Reporting

All queries go to `POST http://localhost:3000/admin-api` with your admin bearer token.

### Query 1 — Search transactions (last 30 days)
```graphql
query {
  paypalTransactions(
    startDate: "2026-05-10T00:00:00Z"
    endDate: "2026-06-09T23:59:59Z"
  ) {
    totalItems
    totalPages
    page
    transactions {
      transactionInfo {
        transactionId
        transactionType
        transactionStatus
        transactionAmount { value currencyCode }
        feeAmount { value currencyCode }
        netAmount { value currencyCode }
        transactionInitiationDate
        invoiceId
      }
      payerInfo {
        emailAddress
        payerName
        countryCode
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Expected:** Returns all PayPal transactions from the last 30 days. Status codes: `S` = success, `V` = reversed (refund), `D` = denied.

### Query 2 — Filter by status (successful only)
```graphql
query {
  paypalTransactions(
    startDate: "2026-05-10T00:00:00Z"
    endDate: "2026-06-09T23:59:59Z"
    transactionStatus: "S"
    pageSize: 10
    page: 1
  ) {
    totalItems
    transactions {
      transactionInfo { transactionId transactionAmount { value currencyCode } }
    }
  }
}
```

### Query 3 — Account balances
```graphql
query {
  paypalAccountBalances {
    accountId
    asOfTime
    balances {
      currency
      primary
      totalBalance { value currencyCode }
      availableBalance { value currencyCode }
      withheldBalance { value currencyCode }
    }
  }
}
```

**Expected:** Returns current balance per currency in the sandbox merchant account.

### Query 4 — Balance at a specific point in time
```graphql
query {
  paypalAccountBalances(asOfTime: "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", currencyCode: "USD") {
    asOfTime
    lastRefreshTime
    balances { currency totalBalance { value currencyCode } }
  }
}
```

### Error cases covered:
- Date range > 31 days → clear error message before hitting PayPal
- Invalid date format → `startDate and endDate must be valid RFC 3339 timestamps`
- endDate before startDate → `endDate must be after startDate`

### Order Tracker Request API

Source: https://github.com/paypal/paypal-typescript-server-sdk/blob/main/doc/models/order-tracker-request.md

Submit tracking details for an order using the Order Tracker Request API.

```APIDOC
## POST /orders/track

### Description
Submits tracking details for an order.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
/orders/track

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **trackingNumber** (string) - Optional - The tracking number for the shipment. This property supports Unicode. Constraints: Minimum Length: 1, Maximum Length: 64
- **carrier** (ShipmentCarrier | undefined) - Optional - The carrier for the shipment. Some carriers have a global version as well as local subsidiaries. The subsidiaries are repeated over many countries and might also have an entry in the global list. Choose the carrier for your country. If the carrier is not available for your country, choose the global version of the carrier. If your carrier name is not in the list, set `carrier` to `OTHER` and set carrier name in `carrier_name_other`. For allowed values, see Carriers. Constraints: Minimum Length: 1, Maximum Length: 64, Pattern: ^[0-9A-Z_]+$
- **carrierNameOther** (string) - Optional - The name of the carrier for the shipment. Provide this value only if the carrier parameter is OTHER. This property supports Unicode. Constraints: Minimum Length: 1, Maximum Length: 64
- **captureId** (string) - Required - The PayPal capture ID. Constraints: Minimum Length: 1, Maximum Length: 50, Pattern: ^[a-zA-Z0-9]*$
- **notifyPayer** (boolean) - Optional - If true, PayPal will send an email notification to the payer of the PayPal transaction. The email contains the tracking details provided through the Orders tracking API request. Independent of any value passed for `notify_payer`, the payer may receive tracking notifications within the PayPal app, based on the user's notification preferences. Default: false
- **items** (OrderTrackerItem[]) - Optional - An array of details of items in the shipment.

### Request Example
{
  "capture_id": "capture_id0",
  "notify_payer": false,
  "tracking_number": "tracking_number6",
  "carrier": "ACS_GR",
  "carrier_name_other": "carrier_name_other0",
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "name8",
      "quantity": "quantity4",
      "sku": "sku6",
      "url": "url2",
      "image_url": "image_url4"
    },
    {
      "name": "name8",
      "quantity": "quantity4",
      "sku": "sku6",
      "url": "url2",
      "image_url": "image_url4"
    }
  ]
}

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **message** (string) - Description of the success response.

#### Response Example
{
  "message": "Tracking details submitted successfully."
}
```

